      "content": "i see. it feels like the school's side is always framed as just being about \"inclusion\" and \"understanding,\" which sounds good on paper. but when people bring up the risks or the way it might affect kids' development, it often gets dismissed as just being \"uninformed\" or \"anti-science.\" do you think the concerns parents have are being given a fair shake in the actual conversation, or is there a tendency to just label those views as outdated?",
